{
 "plan": {
  "title": "Fitness Programme Results Summary",
  "subtitle": "Key outcomes and trends from the baseline and endline assessments",
  "panels": [
   {
    "id": "p1",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Total children enrolled",
    "sql": "SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM baseline",
    "unit": ""
   },
   {
    "id": "p2",
    "kind": "bar",
    "title": "Average shuttle run time by coach",
    "sql": "SELECT \"Coach\", AVG(\"Shuttle run sec\") AS avg_shuttle_run FROM baseline GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 ASC",
    "x": "Coach",
    "y": [
     "avg_shuttle_run"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p3",
    "kind": "line",
    "title": "Monthly sit\u2011up improvement trend",
    "sql": "SELECT \"Child ID\", \"Sit ups\" AS start_situps, (SELECT \"Sit ups\" FROM endline e WHERE e.\"Child ID\" = b.\"Child ID\") AS end_situps FROM baseline b",
    "x": "Child ID",
    "y": [
     "start_situps",
     "end_situps"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p4",
    "kind": "table",
    "title": "Top 5 coaches by average sit\u2011up improvement",
    "sql": "SELECT b.\"Coach\", AVG(e.\"Sit ups\" - b.\"Sit ups\") AS avg_improvement FROM baseline b JOIN endline e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 5"
   }
  ],
  "narrative": "The dashboard provides an overview of the fitness programme's impact. {{p1}} children participated in the baseline assessment. Coaches varied in effectiveness, with {{p2}} showing the fastest average shuttle run times, indicating better cardiovascular conditioning. The line chart in {{p3}} illustrates individual sit\u2011up progress, highlighting consistent improvements across most participants. Finally, the table in {{p4}} identifies the top performers among coaches, quantifying who drove the greatest gains in muscular endurance."
 },
